{"step_index":196,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-18T19:02:03Z","thinking":"**Constructing Modules for Project**\n\nOkay, I'm now focusing on building the modules. I'm starting with `hapticsService.ts`, aiming for a cross-platform haptic sensory engine, using `expo-haptics` natively on iOS/Android and falling back to the Web vibration API. After that, I'll be working on `timeZoneService.ts`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import { Platform } from 'react-native';\n\nexport class HapticsService {\n  private static hapticsModule: any = null;\n\n  private static async getModule() {\n    if (this.hapticsModule) return this.hapticsModule;\n    if (Platform.OS !== 'web') {\n      try {\n        this.hapticsModule = await import('expo-haptics');\n      } catch (e) {\n        // Fallback\n      }\n    }\n    return this.hapticsModule;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Light tap (used for UI buttons, tab changes, and countdown ticks)\n   */\n  static async tick() {\n    try {\n      const Haptics = await this.getModule();\n      if (Haptics) {\n        await Haptics.impactAsync(Haptics.ImpactFeedbackStyle.Light);\n      } else if (typeof navigator !== 'undefined' && navigator.vibrate) {\n        navigator.vibrate(10);\n      }\n    } catch {}\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Medium impact (used for initiating calls, sending texts)\n   */\n  static async medium() {\n    try {\n      const Haptics = await this.getModule();\n      if (Haptics) {\n        await Haptics.impactAsync(Haptics.ImpactFeedbackStyle.Medium);\n      } else if (typeof navigator !== 'undefined' && navigator.vibrate) {\n        navigator.vibrate(25);\n      }\n    } catch {}\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Heavy impact / Warning (used for Bad Number, Disqualify)\n   */\n  static async heavy() {\n    try {\n      const Haptics = await this.getModule();\n      if (Haptics) {\n        await Haptics.impactAsync(Haptics.ImpactFeedbackStyle.Heavy);\n      } else if (typeof navigator !== 'undefined' && navigator.vibrate) {\n        navigator.vibrate([30, 50, 30]);\n      }\n    } catch {}\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Success notification (used for Connected / Qualified)\n   */\n  static async success() {\n    try {\n      const Haptics = await this.getModule();\n      if (Haptics) {\n        await Haptics.notificationAsync(Haptics.NotificationFeedbackType.Success);\n      } else if (typeof navigator !== 'undefined' && navigator.vibrate) {\n        navigator.vibrate([15, 30, 60]);\n      }\n    } catch {}\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Error notification\n   */\n  static async error() {\n    try {\n      const Haptics = await this.getModule();\n      if (Haptics) {\n        await Haptics.notificationAsync(Haptics.NotificationFeedbackType.Error);\n      } else if (typeof navigator !== 'undefined' && navigator.vibrate) {\n        navigator.vibrate([50, 30, 50]);\n      }\n    } catch {}\n  }\n}\n","Description":"Sensory Haptic feedback service with native iOS/Android expo-haptics and web fallbacks","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\services\\hapticsService.ts","toolAction":"Writing haptics service","toolSummary":"Write HapticsService.ts"}}]}
